{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403110-2ed-update-hedgespun-automatons","id":1403110,"title":"[2ed Update] Hedgespun Automatons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-16T09:57:45-07:00","id":1403110,"title":"[2ed Update] Hedgespun Automatons","content":"Consult page 141 of Rites Of Spring for the original version of this system.<br /> <br /> Spend 1 Glamour and roll for a Crafting Equipment Action [ChroD Page 100], with bonus dice equal to your Wyrd. Relevant Specialties and Areas Of Expertise also apply. Certain Contracts, Tokens, Hedgespinning, Goblin Fruit, Merits, Blessing &amp; Trickery of Kiths and so forth can help with the creation of the automaton, usually by providing the adequate materials and tools (e.g. Hollow's Workshop), or removing obstacles and limitations (e.g. Tatterdemalion's Workshop).<br /> <br /> Hedgespun Automatons can only be created inside the Hedge, and the Skill depends on the type of automaton. Examples: Crafts for assembling clockwork soldiers, Medicine for stitching together homunculi, Occult for reciting magical chants to animate puppets, or Expression to create artworks that harvest Glamour from the emotions of observers. The Kith Blessing applies for the purposes of Exceptional Success with 3 Successes, as long as it enhances the same Skill used for creating the automaton.<br /> <br /> For each -1 you take to your dice pool, your robot counts as a Retainer worth 1 dot (up to 5 dots), which also gives them free Merit Dots equal to [Retainer Rating X 2]. This includes Changeling Merits at the ST's discretion, but not ones like Court Mantle, Parallel Lives or Touchstones. The automaton lasts indefinitely, but each one has a battery of Glamour equal to your [Skill] X 2, can spend as many points of Glamour per turn as the Changeling, and starts with the 1 Glamour spent upon rolling. If the Changeling has a relevant Specialty, this battery is increased to [Skill + 1] X 2, and if he has a relevant Area Of Expertise, it is increased to [Skill + 2] X 2. They do not have a Willpower Pool.<br /> <br /> Each automaton depletes 1 Glamour per week of functioning inside of the Hedge, or 1 Glamour per day when within Ironside, and goes dormant without Glamour. Each automaton must be refueled manually through your own points of Glamour, which does not require a roll but takes 1 minute per point of Glamour. Each automaton has access to one Common Arcadian Contract possessed by the creator, and 1 suitable Dread Power, or 1 Numen, or 1 dot of Influence.<br /> <br /> This does not include any powers that would make it impossible to permanently destroy the automaton (e.g. Immortal), would allow it to grant others permanent traits without the expenditure of XP nor narrative tasks (e.g. Miracle), or are exclusive to specific entities (e.g. Resurrection Numen). The automaton has the same Seeming as the creator for the purposes of Affinity benefits in their Contracts, and its activation dice pool for its powers is [Retainer Rating X 2] + [Creator's Wyrd]. If targeted by a supernatural ability, the Hedgespun Automaton contests it with [Retainer Rating + Creator's Wyrd].<br /> <br /> The Changeling can give additional features by taking more penalties to his dice pool on a 1 for 1 ratio, usually in the form of Merits or Merit-like properties. The Changeling does not need to have such Merits himself to include them in the automaton. The creation roll takes one day per -1 taken, before factoring bonuses. Consider using Fae Mounts and Hedgespun Items as guidelines for the features of automatons.Teamwork with other Changelings can reduce the time taken in proportion to the Successes of the secondary actors: every 2 Successes offer a reduction of 1 day, rounded down.<br /> <br /> When creating an automaton, the main actor must decide whether Teamwork gives bonus dice OR reduces the time taken. Every automaton possesses Durability equal to [Skill], but does not heal Structure Damage passively.Therefore, a Changeling must Repair it, and their dice pool for Repairing receives bonus dice equal to their Wyrd. Each -1 imposed on this roll removes 1 Structure Damage, and takes 1 hour. If the automation is biological or made of components that are comparable to living tissue, then it heals Health Damage passively like a mortal would, but does not benefit from the inherent damage reduction of Durability. Cold Iron bypasses all Durability, Armor, and mystical protections of an automaton, and deals Aggravated Damage, like it does to Changelings.<br /> <br /> You can have up to your [Wyrd] in active Hedgespun Automatons simultaneously, but you can store inactive automatons inside your Hollow or equivalently secure location. Automatons cannot regain Glamour on their own unless the creator includes an ability or property that allows it. Even so, automatons might struggle or cause problems if attempting to regain Glamour via Emotions if their Retainer purview is not focused on social interaction, and so forth for other methods of regaining Glamour. Discovering how to create a specific model of automaton is its own process, which usually requires an Extended Action of some sort. As a suggestion: Intelligence + Occult, Target Successes = [Total Dice Penalty Imposed Onto The Crafting Equipment Roll] X 2, one hour per roll, with Merits like Library being applicable.<br /> <br /> For automatons whose designs are especially difficult, the ST can request that creating blueprints or equivalent documentation requires something more involved, such as haggling in a specialized Goblin Market, Uncovering Clues through the Hedge, seeking Dream Beings to request inspirational ideas, and so forth. Huntsmen can capture and analyze these automatons to identify the magical thumbprints and tells of the Changeling, and follow that clue through the ebb and flow of the Wyrd until they find their prey.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Huntsman gains bonus dice to find and capture the Changeling equal to the automaton's Retainer Rating, which also applies to activating their supernatural powers, including Hedgespinning. Hedgespun Automatons tend to become gradually stranger as time passes, especially if exposed to excessive damage, abuse or neglect. The Changeling must perform inspections and maintenance on his automatons at least once per Chapter to make sure they do not develop beyond their base programming, which takes 15 minutes per automaton.<br /> <br /> An Exceptional Success on the roll to create an automaton gives it the capacity to understand and follow complex instructions that would normally confuse it and lead to dangerous choices based on its misinterpretation. Furthermore, the Exceptional Success grants additional Common Arcadian Contracts and/or Dread Powers equal to the Changeling's [Wyrd/2 Rounded Up].<br /> <br /> Creating Hedgespun Art uses the same mechanics as Hedgespun Automatons. The Skill used by the creator is usually Expression, and the artwork rolls a dice pool of [Retainer Rating X 2] to cause a specific type of emotion, such as anger toward authorities, fear toward spiders, carnal desire, or sorrow of lost opportunities. This has the same suggested modifiers for when a Changeling personally harvests Glamour from an emotion. Other modifiers are also possible, especially if the observer has a Virtue/Vice, Needle/Thread, Aspiration or Condition which makes him more susceptible to being emotionally influenced by the artwork.<br /> <br /> The artwork starts with 1 Common Court Contract possessed by the creator, and 1 Dread Power or 1 Numen or 1 Influence dot, all of which must be based on emotional influence. The artwork uses [Retainer Rating X 2] + [Creator's Court Mantle] as its dice pool for activating its Common Court Contracts, but it cannot acquire any Physical or Mental Merits, and neither can it physically affect the observer in a direct way. However, it can emotionally influence him to make decisions with physical consequences.<br /> <br /> On a Success, the artwork can harvest Glamour from the emotion it causes in the observer. Each Success scored by the artwork drains 1 Glamour, and removes 1 Willpower Point from the observer, as per the usual mechanics for harvesting Glamour from emotions. The creator or another Changeling can retrieve this Glamour by simply touching the artwork (or the object that produces/contains the artistic experience, in the case of mediums like music and movies).<br /> <br /> If the creator has the Fair Harvest Merit, its benefits also apply to the roll of the artwork. On an Exceptional Success for making the artwork, it can harvest Glamour from an emotion in its entirety, and it has additional Common Court Contracts and/or Dread Powers equal to the Changeling's [Wyrd/2 Rounded Up]. Any emotions caused by the artwork's powers cannot be used as a source of Glamour, as usual. Changelings can notice that the artwork is supernatural via Kenning, Goblin's Eye and equivalent powers, which is not contested nor resisted.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural entities can accomplish this with their powers of detection. Supernatural attempts to remove or alter the emotions caused by the artwork are contested by [Retainer Rating] + [Creator's Wyrd], and mundane attempts are penalized by [Retainer Rating]. The artwork uses its own reserves of Glamour to activate its Contracts, and can spend up to [Creator's Wyrd] Glamour at once for this activation.<br /> <br /> As compensation for not being able to physically affect the observer in a direct way, the artwork does not need regular maintenance like an automaton does, and the Changeling is not subject to the limit of [Wyrd] active instances that applies to automatons. In order to include Common Contracts he does not possess himself in the automaton or artwork, he must swear an Oath to another Changeling who possess such Contracts. This Oath must be related to cooperation with tasks within the purview of the [Skill] used to create the automaton or artwork.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hodgepodge Designs Style (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> Prerequisites: Changeling<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Gain bonus dice for creating Hedgespun Automatons/Artworks equal to [Style Rating]. Furthermore, add [Style Rating] to [Wyrd] to determine the maximum number of simultaneously active automatons, and add [Style Rating] to any Social roll the Changeling makes to harvest Glamour if he personally uses the artwork in some way to cause the emotion.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): The Hedgespun Automatons acquire a Willpower Pool equal to [Retainer Rating], as well as a Virtue and a Vice if the creator wants, which are selected by the creator and allow the automatons to replenish Willpower Points like a mortal world. However, these Virtues and Vices do not have to match the ones typically displayed by mortals (e.g. Justice or Wrath)<br /> <br /> However, since the automaton lacks Clarity or Integrity, it will likely fulfill its Virtue or indulge its Vice in literal-minded ways, with the only rules being the ones chosen by the Changeling when creating the automaton. Hedgespun Artworks instead acquire the capacity to Incite Bedlam, using its [Retainer Rating X 2] as its dice pool and being subject to the same suggested modifiers for when a Changeling personally Incites Bedlam.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): All rolls to create Hedgespun Automatons/Artworks achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever the Changeling scores an Exceptional Success to create the automaton or artwork, it acquires additional Common Contracts / Dread Powers / Numina / Influence Dots equal to [Creator's Wyrd + Style Rating/2 Rounded Up].<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Once per Story, you may suffer 1 Severe Clarity Damage and sacrifice 1 Willpower DOT when creating a Hedgespun Automaton. This imbues it with sapience and free will, with all that entails. For example: subjectively interpreting commands, making independent decisions, learning dynamically and generally demonstrating agency. This person can be represented as a full-fledged Hobgoblin with a Wyrd equal to [Creator's Wyrd/2 Rounded Up], but barring truly extreme or unusual circumstances, it does not acquire Clarity.<br /> <br /> Creating life like this is almost always a Breaking Point for Clarity if it is done with the intent to enslave, abuse, imprison or otherwise treat the person like a Gentry would. If the Changeling finds a suitable Icon in the Hedge and sacrifices it without boosting her Clarity, he does not have to sacrifice 1 Willpower DOT. Furthermore, once per Story, you may suffer 1 Severe Clarity Damage and sacrifice 1 Willpower DOT when creating a Hedgespun Artwork to give it the capacity to physically and directly affect the observer with its powers, as if the observer is being targeted by an Oneiromantic action while suffering from the Flesh Too Solid Tilt. This can likewise make the creator and the observer suffer from relevant Clarity Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> If the Changeling finds a suitable Bauble in the Dreamlands [Swords At Dawn Pages 114 To 117], and uses it as part of an Oneiromantic action inside his own dreams that enacts a Paradigm-Shift related to the nature of the artwork, he does not have to sacrifice 1 Willpower DOT. The Changeling can keep the Bauble and use it normally after using it for this Paradigm-Shift. If the Changeling gives up an Icon or makes use of a Bauble, and sacrifices a Willpower DOT regardless, he can change the Loopholes of the automaton's or the artwork's Common Contracts, including those imitated by swearing an Oath to another Changeling. However, each such changed Loophole incurs 1 point of Goblin Debt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-07-2022, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T15:11:50-07:00","id":1403719,"title":"","content":"I rather like this. I was a little sad that Hedgespun Automatons weren\u2019t really a thing anymore due to how Hedgespinning now works, so this idea is quite welcome.<br /> <br /> Slightly off topic but still related, I actually have been working on an Entitlement that allows one to breathe life into hedge crafted puppets, turning them into hobgoblins who are bound to be loyal to the bearer for a year and a day before freeing them to live their lives in the Hedge. This merit style and these rules could benefit my homebrew Entitlement rather nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T22:03:30-07:00","id":1403763,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403110-2ed-update-hedgespun-automatons#post1403110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consult page 141 of Rites Of Spring for the original version of this system.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> wonderful job! Hope you don't mind that I took what you did and made this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Hedge Topiaries</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">While the Hedge provide opportunities for miraculous craftmanship, it also is an environment which is often verdantly lush and can be cultivated as a source of Glamour. Using Hedgespinning and cultivation to alter the plants of the Hedge can result in hedge plants shaped like animals, people or fantastical beasts which grow Goblin Fruit which it may use as a supernatural fuel source to animate and obey their cultivator. Hedge Topiaries possess different strengths and weaknesses than Hedgespun Automatons and the creation methods also differs to be not solely a matter of finesse and requires either dedication to cultivation of the Hedge or equal mastery of both cultivation and occult practices.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spend 1 Glamour and roll [Presence, Dexterity, or Resolve] + (lower of Occult or Survival) + Wyrd as an Crafting Equipment Action [ChroD Page 100]. Changeling who use Resolve approach it through fastidious researched and painstaking control of the metaphysical influences where the plant is cultivated. Those who use Dexterity approach this through clever grafting and pruning of appropriate vine or branch varieties. Finally, those who use Presence prick their thumb upon a hedge thorn to water a seedling with a drop of their blood while sincerely opening up their heart to the growing sprout, and over the growing time earnestly crooning regardless of talent to their darling little seedling surrogate baby. For each -1 you take to your dice pool, your animated hedge plant counts as a Retainer worth 1 dot (up to 5 dots). The field of the Retainer is chosen at the time of cultivation, such examples as acting as a sentry (perhaps it is a thorny stab-apple bush shaped like a giant lion), getting you money (perhaps it literally growing money like leaves or seed pods), making the Hollow pleasant (perhaps it is a juniper like bush shaped as a maid with wonderfully fragrant flowery vines) or acting as a covert scout (a small collection of bristly vines in the shape of an oriental dragon capable of maneuvering into hard to reach passages). The plants you magically nurture only last for one hour per Success, unless you also spend 1 Willpower to make them last indefinitely (which does not add dice). Each one grows a maximum number of Goblin fruits equal to the lower of your Occult or Survival, can willfully wither a fruit that is still attached as a way of spending Glamour {limited to as many points per turn as its cultivator). At the end of the initial Cultivation of its creation it has a single Goblin Fruit after it animates. Every day it spends any time animated depletes 1 Goblin Fruit and the plant involuntarily goes dormant when it is without its daily dose of Glamour from its own unpicked Goblin Fruit. Additionally these hedgespun creations have a very strong tie to the Hedge, essentially being an animated part of it, and universally have a Bane of being outside the Hedge, instantly withering all attached Goblin Fruits and suffering Aggravated damage each turn as it shrivels to unidentifiable dessicated mulch. These plants grow back a single Goblin Fruit each day it spends rooted at least an hour in a place within the Hollow whose conditions do not prohibit Goblin Fruit from potentially growing. The plant may remain dormant deliberately to build a reserve of Goblin Fruit, and while dormant it remains aware of its surroundings but may not animate until it depletes an attached Goblin Fruit (a reflexive action). Once a Hedgespun Topiary is at maximum capacity for Goblin Fruit they cease growing fruit even if suitable location until a Goblin Fruit is picked from it or it depletes a Goblin Fruit. If a Hollow has more Hedge Topiaries grow their daily Goblin Fruit than the Hollow's Rating it gains the </span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403756-2e-environmental-tilt-glamour-barren-hedge-based#post1403756\">Glamour Barren Environmental Tilt</a><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. Each plant has access to one Common Arcadian Contract, which you must possess yourself. This Contract can vary between plants, and the activation dice pool is [Retainer Rating X 2]. If targeted by a supernatural ability, the Hedgespun Topiary contests it with [Retainer Rating + Wyrd of the Changeling]. After the initial creation of the Hedgespun Topiary it no longer is able to a</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The creation roll takes one day. With a suitable Specialty, this is shortened to one hour, which is in addition to the +1 die of the Specialty. If your Specialty is also an Area Of Expertise, this is further reduced to one minute, which is in addition to the +2 dice of the Expert Specialty. Every plant possesses Durability equal to the lower of your Occult or Survival, but if struck with Cold Iron it is immediately destroyed. The Changeling can give the plant additional features by taking more penalties to his dice pool, on a 1 for 1 ratio. Use the features of Fae Mount Merit as guidelines. Incorporating components from the Hedge which match the design and intended function of the plant can give bonus dice. There is no hard limit for how many Hedgespun Topiaries you can have, other than the toll they can take upon the Goblin Fruit growing capacities they have upon Hollows. However, certain Huntsmen can capture and compost these plants to grow a flowerbed which blooms as a portrait of the Changeling nurturer, and follow that clue through the ebb and flow of the Wyrd until they find their prey. Furthermore, even without applying the 5th Maneuver of the following Style, Hedgespun Topiaries tend to become gradually stranger as time passes. The Changeling must not only reap the harvest of their labor and fruit them, but inspect them to prune them so they don't grow to become unruly through lack of careful cultivation and make sure they do not develop behavior altering pests or parasites.</span><br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Hedge Cultivation Style (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Prerequisites: Changeling</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">You are exceptionally talented at building Hedgespun Topiaries of various kinds, from massive and sturdy treant-like Goblin Fruit trees to lithe and agile ambulatory collections of thorned vines in the shape as artistic a small oriental dragon. Using this Style requires the Changeling to be inside a Hollow equipped with a suitable Workshop, but the Hollow need not belong to him.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(\u2022): Gain bonus dice for creating Hedgespun Topiaries equal to [Style Rating].</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(\u2022\u2022): When cultivating Hedgespun Topiaries all references to the lower of Occult or Survival of the cultivator instead become the higher of Occult or Survival of the Cultivator (including maximum Goblin Fruits per Hedge Topiary), and they become lasting without the need to spend 1 Willpower.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022): All rolls to create Hedgespun Topiaries gain Rote Quality. Whenever you achieve an Exceptional Success to build a Hedgespun Topiary, the Goblin Fruits it will bear are of a particular variety which have effects beyond merely granting Glamour to the consumer. The precise variety must be in the possession of the creator, and one piece of that type of Goblin Fruit is expended in the creation.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Hedgespun Topiaries have access to one Royal Arcadian Contract you possess, which is in addition to the Common Arcadian Contract.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Once per Chapter, you may suffer 1 Severe Clarity Damage when building a Hedgespun Topiary. This imbues it with self-awareness, allowing it to subjectively interpret commands, make independent decisions and learn dynamically. This makes the creature stand out in the eyes of the Wyrd, which significantly increases the risk of it obtaining true agency and transforming into a full-fledged Hobgoblin.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403756-2e-environmental-tilt-glamour-barren-hedge-based#post1403756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\"><i><b>Tilt</b></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Glamour Barren</b></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Environmental <i>(Hedge locations only)</i></b></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Description:</b> This particular area of the Hedge has be depleted of the supernatural energy needed for Goblin Fruits, or Hedge plants to grow.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Effect:</b> Goblin Fruits will not grow in this area, nor will the plants which bear them sprout. Hedgespinning, cultivation and Contracts cannot cause plant sprouting, growth, rejuvenation, blooming, fruiting or ripening withing an area with this Condition. Effects including Hedgespinning and Contracts can still cause wilting, withering, rot of plants in the area, and for that purpose achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success. This does not prohibit the Hedge's ability to cause Thorns to inflict the area, merely means those Thorns will not be plant based and there will be no Goblin Fruit. Also if a being which are not manifestations of Thorns gives birth in the area, the offspring is either stillborn for beings without Souls, or born with the Soulless Condition if the being would normally have a soul.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Over exploitation of Goblin Fruit cultivation or Hedgespinning Goblin Fruits into existence too often in the area, Interruptions to the cycle of Glamour renewal within the area, Effects with leech all ambient Glamour from the area</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ending the Tilt:</b> If caused by over exploitation of Goblin Fruit then the area must be dutifully tended to for a year and a day as though it was fallow ground for cultivation as the first half of ending the Tilt. If caused by interruptions to Glamour renewal is the cause then those interruptions must be stopped, and the same goes for effects which leech all ambient Glamour from the area. After the first half of the resolution is completed fertilizing the affected with the ashes from a giant Wickerman which burns a living fae creature with a Soul trapped inside to death as a sacrifice finally ends this Tilt.</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-21-2020, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T05:26:00-07:00","id":1403982,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> I love this a whole lot. Though in my opinion there is no real need for a separate Merit and such. I would just let the player use Medicine instead of Crafts, and change the particulars of the system accordingly. I say Medicine because it gives technical and methodical knowledge of biology, while Survival is more about practical and immediate knowledge of various bits of geography, hunting and such. There is no tangible benefit for requiring an additional expenditure of 5 XP if you can simply reflavor the mechanics, you know? You definitely gave me ideas for a certain NPC of mine, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-22-2020, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T14:27:26-08:00","id":1498639,"title":"","content":"Wrote a major revision for the original post. Constructive feedback is welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T19:13:00-08:00","id":1498811,"title":"","content":"Added rules for Hedgespun Art as well, and expanded the Hodgepodge Blueprints Style to also help with creating 